A||||5||walsh2001||Fiero Woes :(||||11||
Z||000000||walsh2001||11-14-2001||09:08 AM||||Allright here are the symptoms:<P>1. Car runs really hard when it is first started for the day (or after being parked all day). It wants to stall when I try to accelerate into first and is jerky. Also, I have the dreaded ticking, almost more of a loud clicking (valves?) when I accelerate or drive up a hill.<P>2. I am hearing wierd noises in the front end. Steering feels loose; it makes weird clicking sounds if start to turn the wheel a little while the car is/ is not moving.<P>3. Ever since I had my clutch replaced... The rear has felt really loose, my wheel bearings have started humming and the car pulls to the right. I went to Big 10 and had them check the alignment: they said it was fine; they had no idea why it was pulling. <P>Please Help!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jason<P>------------------<BR>'87 Fiero GT ... Cherry Red||||reg||11
Z||000001||JohnF||11-14-2001||09:25 AM||||Pulling can be from many things.  <P>If alignment is good, I would strongly suspect the tires themselves.  Wrong rotation, different sizes, different pressures (side-to-side) and even wrong tires.  <P>Try swapping tires around and see if there is a difference.  Yeah, I know we are supposed to go fore-and-aft with swaps but around-and-around will tell if there is a tire problem quickly.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||11-14-2001||09:54 AM||||The ticking under load is most likely an exhaust leak fairly close to the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||reddog||11-15-2001||07:49 PM||||If its pulling to the right you might want to check the brakes. Could be a caliper is stuck. The ticking is probably an exhaust leak at the manifold. BTW it's an unwritten rule that if you have an exhuast leak it will always be on the firewall side because it would be too easy to fix if it were on the truckside.just kidding!! Also check plugs and wires, Timming could also be off!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||reddog||11-15-2001||07:58 PM||||OH YEAH If you haven't replaced your coolant temp. sensor, try that. If it goes bad it will make the car run crappy and will stall. It will run like Sh*t until the engine warms up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ITB 2M4||11-15-2001||11:56 PM||||You might also want to check that they got the half-shafts all the way into the trans.  If one is under power and the other is just attached to the wheel, it will pull, but only while on the gas.  Since you had the clutch replaced, they probably had the engine cradle off the car.  The alignment might be fine when the car is stationary on a machine, but when various forces (accel., braking, turning) act on the car, something loose like a strut, or drive axle nut can really move around.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
